"""Foot-contact point set of the Neura 4NE1 G3.3 model. GENERATED -- do not edit.

Regenerate with ``python scripts/dev/export_4ne1_g3_3_xml.py`` after a CAD re-export;
``tests/test_neura_4ne1_model.py`` fails if this table is stale.

The points are the vertices of the compiled MuJoCo collision hulls of both feet
(``{side}_foot_collision``, ``maxhullvert=64``), expressed in the ``link_{side}_ankle_x``
body frame (the welded ``sensor_*_foot_fts`` body has an identity transform), plus
their y-mirrors, so ONE table bounds either foot: the lowest world point of a foot
under any rotation is one of its hull vertices, hence ``clip_min_sole`` (which pins
the lowest of these points to z=0 per clip) never leaves a foot inside the floor.
The left/right hulls differ by up to ~1 cm laterally, so the mirrored copies make
the table conservative by at most that much under large roll angles.
"""

